# Test: show mtu host measures one clamped path and names how
# Spec: spec-path-mtu-diagnostic -- user story 2, AC-1
# VALIDATES: an operator runs `show mtu host 10.99.2.1` over a path whose middle
#            router clamps its far link to 1400. The payload's one measurement
#            targets that address, carries path-mtu 1400 found `via ICMP`, names
#            the underlay interface the route leaves by, carries no inventory,
#            verdict or reference key, and `detail` lists every probe sent.
# PREVENTS: a host run that consults the tunnel inventory, a measurement whose
#           method is a zero, and a figure reported that the wire never confirmed.
#
# The path is three network namespaces joined by veth pairs, built by the
# compiled fixture `plugin/clamped-path` (internal/test/fixture, netlink): the
# daemon runs in the sender namespace, the router forwards with its far link at
# 1400, and the far namespace answers. Building them needs CAP_NET_ADMIN and
# the raw ICMP socket needs CAP_NET_RAW, so the test runs in the QEMU guest as
# root (`./le qemu all-tests`) and skips in the unprivileged merge gate. The
# fixture removes the namespaces when the daemon exits, whatever its exit code.

option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin,net-raw
option=env:var=ze.storage.blob:value=false

tmpfs=mtu-host.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external show-mtu-test {
		run "ze-test fixture plugin/show-mtu-host"
		encoder json
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture plugin/clamped-path netns zemtuhost$PORT run ze start mtu-host.conf:timeout=60s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: show mtu host measured the clamp at 1400 via ICMP over sr0
reject=stderr:pattern=ZE-OBSERVER-FAIL
reject=stderr:pattern=panic recovered
